# Graphify

This repo has a local knowledge graph at `graphify-out/` (AST-built, no API key required for code).

## When to use it first

Before broad codebase exploration (architecture questions, “what depends on X”, cross-module flow):

```bash
# Ensure CLI is on PATH (uv tool):
# $env:PATH = "C:\Users\amzad\.local\bin;$env:PATH"

graphify query "<question>"
graphify path "<SymbolA>" "<SymbolB>"
graphify explain "<concept>"
graphify god-nodes --top 15
```

Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` for a high-level community map, or open `graphify-out/graph.html` in a browser.

## When to skip straight to Read/Grep

- You already know the file path and are editing or debugging a specific line
- `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing (rebuild with `graphify extract . --code-only`)
- Narrow symbol lookup inside a single known file

## Keep the graph fresh

After substantial code changes:

```bash
graphify update .
```

Git post-commit / post-checkout hooks refresh the AST graph automatically when installed (`graphify hook install`).

Docs/PDF semantic extraction is optional later (`graphify extract .` with an LLM backend); day-to-day use `--code-only` / `update`.
